index b782d5d380..9df490879b 100644
--- a/public/live/readme.md
+++ b/public/live/readme.md
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ Reading never writes a line. `page_read(path)` is the whole page as text. `item(
 - **Tabs are this page's own content; link cards go elsewhere.** A tab is a sub-page that draws as part of this page: a plain LivePage folder with no pages of its own. Switching tabs keeps the same tab row and the same h1 (the parent's title; the selected tab says which one). Everything else is a **link card** under the content (`LivePage.Pages`, drawn by code, never written into page.jsonl): a sub-page with pages of its own, a page of another class (DesignPage, a `page.js`), a page that says `{"tab": false}` (a small app, like /live/lab/), and every saved screen. More than five tabs would be a list, so then every sub-page is a card (`LivePage.tab_max`). /live/sessions/, /live/archive/ and /live/v1/ are neither (`LivePage.tab_skip`); the footer of /live/ links them. The rule is `LivePage.pages_of`.
 - **One title everywhere:** a tab label, a link card's title and the page's own h1 all read the sub-page's own `title` (the last `title` in its `page.jsonl`, else its `page.js`; `LivePage.title_of`). To rename a sub-page, set its title on its own path: `item({path: "/live/demos/", delta: {"title": "Feature demos"}})`. A link card's `title` shows only until the page's own one arrives.
 - **The breadcrumb is the url** (`location.pathname`, word for word, every step a link): a phone hides the address bar, so this is where the owner reads it. It redraws on every url change, a tab switch included (`LivePage.on_url`), and the tab row lights the tab the url is in.
-- **Settings** (the gear, `<page>/settings/`): where the page's data comes from (its own `page.jsonl`, a card or saved screen inside the parent's `page.jsonl`, or a `page.js`), its class and line count, and the folder's files, one list top to bottom: folders, then files (`LivePage.Files`). A folder opens its own list (`/live/settings/doc/`); a file opens its text on its own page, highlighted by ext/highlight and wrapped to the screen (`/live/settings/LivePage.css/`). A folder or a saved screen named `settings` wins over it.
+- **Settings** (the gear, `<page>/settings/`): where the page's data comes from (its own `page.jsonl`, a card or saved screen inside the parent's `page.jsonl`, or a `page.js`), its class and line count, and the folder's files, one list top to bottom: folders, then files (`LivePage.Files`). A folder opens its own list (`/live/settings/doc/`); a file opens its text on its own page, highlighted by ext/highlight and wrapped to the screen (`/live/settings/LivePage.css/`). A folder or a saved screen named `settings` wins over it. Below that: "What it is made of" and "How it got here" — [ext/Inspect](/framework/ext/Inspect/readme.md)'s `ItemInspector` (its content, methods, fields) and `DeltaHistory` (a slider replaying the folder's `page.jsonl` in memory), both loaded only once settings opens.
